    "title": "WHO 5th paediatric extragonadal germ cell tumours & COG staging",
    "intro": "Thorough sampling (at least 1 block/cm of solid/fleshy areas) is critical in sacrococcygeal and mediastinal teratomas to exclude microscopic foci of yolk sac tumour. Coccygectomy is mandatory for Stage I sacrococcygeal primaries.",
    "note": "Photomicrographs are from Wikimedia Commons under open Creative Commons licences. ExpertPath pages open with your own ExpertPath login; the app holds none of their images.",
    "groups": [
     {
      "heading": "Component identification, immature grading & COG staging",
      "points": [
       "Immature teratoma grade (Gonzalez-Crussi / Norris): Grade 1 <= 1 LPF immature neuroectoderm per slide; Grade 2 = 2–3 LPF; Grade 3 >= 4 LPF. Always exclude microscopic yolk sac tumour (SALL4+, glypican-3+, AFP+).",
       "COG Stage I = complete resection with negative margins (and coccygectomy for sacrococcygeal) and normalising markers; Stage II = microscopic residual; Stage III = gross residual or regional nodal metastasis; Stage IV = distant metastasis."
